    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_20051211.0341\n\nATHENS, Dec 11 , 2005\n\ncharges\n\n\n\n\nCoastguard officials at the main Greek port of Piraeus have arrested the Bulgarian second engineer of a British-flagged tanker sought on manslaughter charges, the Greek merchant marine ministry said Sunday.\n\nVladimir Bankov, 39, will be taken to a prosecutor in the northern city of Salonika under a local warrant issued in 2000, a ministry source told AFP.\n\nBankov, a second engineer on board the British-flagged Zim Shenzhen, is accused of premeditated manslaughter, the source said.\n\nThe ministry did not provide any further details on the crime case.",
